Intercom is a simple voice over IP (VOIP) utility for Unix systems.  It
supports various audio compression formats as well as different sample
rates, enabling the user to choose between high-quality or low-throughput. 
It was primarily designed to provide higher audio quality over fast
connections than the available Linux utilities at the time.  Intercom is a
console application with a command interface.

Version 0.11 is the first public release of this utility and I consider it
to be alpha quality code.  However, feedback is appreciated.

